• Support month-end and year-end close process; 
• Review the periodic bank reconciliations and balance sheet reconciliations;  
• Conducting webinars for the Group entities related to new policies and accounting standards; and • Research technical accounting issues for compliance

I am mainly responsible for drafting current and future forecasted cash flows, reporting budget and variance analysis to the M.D., development of Standard Operating Policies and Procedures and conducting internal controls reviews, reviewing and auditing receipts and payments, regularly reviewing the work of the Accounts Department, and monitoring the journal entries and the overall accounting system.

I have additional responsibility of negotiating, drafting and finalizing contracts with the sub-contractors and suppliers of ‘Marina 101’ in line with the budget.

Moreover, I am also responsible for handling all financial matters of our upcoming Hotel, Hard Rock Hotel (HRH) Dubai Marina. In particular, I have been involved in the finalizations of Pre-Opening Budget (POB), Operating Supplies and Equipments (OS&E) Budget, A.V/I.T Budget and Budget of Fit-out works of HRH Dubai Marina with Hard Rock International and GM HRH Dubai Marina.

Furthermore, I am also responsible for reviewing suppliers’ contracts and cash flows of SHL’s Sister companies and ensure the financial records of all other projects of Sheffield Group are up-to-date.

Other responsibilities include:

